name: sim.unpackDoubleTable
description: Unpacks a string (or part of it) into an array of double floating-point numbers
luaSynopsis: list doubleNumbers = sim.unpackDoubleTable(bytes data, int startDoubleIndex = 0, int doubleCount = 0, int additionalByteOffset = 0)
pythonSynopsis: float[] doubleNumbers = sim.unpackDoubleTable(buffer data, int startDoubleIndex = 0, int doubleCount = 0, int additionalByteOffset = 0)
inputs:
1. data: string (values between 0 and 255) that contains packed floating-point numbers
2. startDoubleIndex: zero-based index from which on data should be unpacked (from data[8*startDoubleIndex+1+additionalByteOffset]). Can be omitted in which case 0 is used
3. doubleCount: amount of doubles that should be unpacked. Can be omitted in which case 0 is used (which indicates that the maximum of doubles should be unpacked from the indicated startIndex)
4. additionalByteOffset: byte offset that will be added before reading the doubless. Can be omitted, in which case 0 is used.
outputs:
1. doubleNumbers: array containing unpacked double floating-point numbers
replacedBy:
- name: unpackArray, class: app, file: app_unpackArray.method
